## Commands I Ran Today

### Step 1: Install PostgreSQL on Windows
- Downloaded installer from: https://www.postgresql.org/download/windows/
- During installation:
  - Port: 5432 (default, kept it)
  - Password: `spotpass123`
  - Locale: Default (kept it)
  - Stack Builder: Cancelled (not needed right now)

### Step 2: Create Database via PowerShell
```powershell
# Connect to PostgreSQL as superuser
& "C:\Program Files\PostgreSQL\17\bin\psql.exe" -U postgres
# Entered password: spotpass123

# Inside psql prompt (postgres=#):
CREATE DATABASE spotdb;
\q
Step 3: Verify Database Exists
powershell
& "C:\Program Files\PostgreSQL\17\bin\psql.exe" -U postgres -d spotdb
# Entered password: spotpass123
# Connected successfully → database exists
\q
Step 4: Create Project Folder Structure
powershell
cd ~                                    # Go to home folder (C:\Users\rkrev)
mkdir spot-app                          # Create main project folder
cd spot-app                             # Enter project folder
git init                                # Initialize git for version control
mkdir backend                           # Create backend folder
cd backend                              # Enter backend folder
Step 5: Set Up Python Virtual Environment
powershell
python -m venv venv                     # Create virtual environment
.\venv\Scripts\Activate                 # Activate it (Windows PowerShell command)
# Terminal now shows (venv) in green at the start
Step 6: Install Python Packages
powershell
pip install fastapi uvicorn sqlalchemy psycopg2-binary python-jose[cryptography] passlib[bcrypt] python-multipart
Step 7: Create First API Endpoint
powershell
mkdir app                               # Create app folder inside backend
notepad app\main.py                     # Open Notepad to create main.py
# Clicked "Yes" when asked to create new file
Pasted into app/main.py:

python
from fastapi import FastAPI

app = FastAPI(title="SPOT", version="0.1.0")

@app.get("/")
def hello():
    return {"message": "SPOT is alive! July 27 done."}
Step 8: Run the Server
powershell
uvicorn app.main:app --reload
app.main = the file app/main.py

:app = the FastAPI instance named "app" inside that file

--reload = automatically restart when code changes

Step 9: Test in Browser
Opened: http://127.0.0.1:8000

Saw: {"message":"SPOT is alive! July 27 done."} ✅

Also visited: http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs — FastAPI's automatic interactive API documentation

Step 10: Stop the Server
text
Ctrl + C (pressed in terminal)
Step 11: Deactivate Virtual Environment
powershell
deactivate
